-- M3 fixes, B1 (O2): `\(` INSIDE a `[...]` class is not a group
-- opener in the Str dialect (a backslash is an ordinary class member
-- there), so this pattern has ZERO groups and the class matches
-- either of the two members `\` and `(`.  Pre-fix the syntactic
-- counter saw one phantom group and Str.matched_group killed the
-- whole process with an uncaught Invalid_argument (exit 2, recorded
-- in dev/M3-FIXES-LOG.md).  dev/gates.sh pins the printed value.
eval regexMatch "[\\(]x" "(x"
